WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.571
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.871 --> 00:00:09.164
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.464 --> 00:00:14.740
Unit twelve: Prepositions of Movement. Today you will describe movement and direction.

4
00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:17.623
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.567 --> 00:00:21.939
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.783 --> 00:00:23.680
Into.

7
00:00:24.683 --> 00:00:26.764
Into means moving to the inside.

8
00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:28.746
She walked into the room.

9
00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:31.619
Your turn. Say: Into.

10
00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:35.201
Into.

11
00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:36.881
Onto.

12
00:00:37.883 --> 00:00:40.103
Onto means moving to the top of something.

13
00:00:40.717 --> 00:00:42.461
The cat jumped onto the table.

14
00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:45.749
Your turn. Say: Onto.

15
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:49.439
Onto.

16
00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:50.906
Through.

17
00:00:51.917 --> 00:00:54.799
Through means from one end to the other inside something.

18
00:00:55.383 --> 00:00:56.988
We walked through the forest.

19
00:00:57.583 --> 00:00:59.725
Your turn. Say: Through.

20
00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:03.521
Through.

21
00:01:04.283 --> 00:01:05.308
Across.

22
00:01:06.317 --> 00:01:08.502
Across means from one side to the other.

23
00:01:09.117 --> 00:01:10.965
We walked across the bridge.

24
00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:14.307
Your turn. Say: Across.

25
00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:18.377
Across.

26
00:01:19.117 --> 00:01:20.013
Along.

27
00:01:21.017 --> 00:01:23.968
Along means following a line, such as a road.

28
00:01:24.583 --> 00:01:26.223
We walked along the river.

29
00:01:26.817 --> 00:01:29.121
Your turn. Say: Along.

30
00:01:31.967 --> 00:01:32.747
Along.

31
00:01:33.483 --> 00:01:34.252
Towards.

32
00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:37.400
Towards means in the direction of something.

33
00:01:38.017 --> 00:01:39.598
He ran towards the gate.

34
00:01:40.183 --> 00:01:42.545
Your turn. Say: Towards.

35
00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:46.308
Towards.

36
00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:47.819
Movement.

37
00:01:48.817 --> 00:01:51.350
Movement means the act of changing place.

38
00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:53.648
Movement keeps us healthy.

39
00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:56.496
Your turn. Say: Movement.

40
00:01:59.333 --> 00:02:00.242
Movement.

41
00:02:00.983 --> 00:02:02.019
Direction.

42
00:02:03.017 --> 00:02:05.411
Direction means the way that something moves.

43
00:02:06.017 --> 00:02:07.993
Which direction is the market?

44
00:02:08.583 --> 00:02:11.073
Your turn. Say: Direction.

45
00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:14.923
Direction.

46
00:02:15.733 --> 00:02:19.686
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:23.699
Visal, describe how you go from your house to school.

48
00:02:24.783 --> 00:02:32.732
I walk along the river, across the bridge and through the park. These are prepositions of movement. They show the path of a journey.

49
00:02:33.817 --> 00:02:36.223
What is the difference between in and into?

50
00:02:37.317 --> 00:02:48.273
In is a position: The cat is in the room. Into is movement: The cat ran into the room. In the same way, on is a position and onto is movement.

51
00:02:49.383 --> 00:02:50.408
And towards?

52
00:02:51.517 --> 00:03:02.461
Towards shows direction, but we may not arrive: He ran towards the gate. Compare to the gate, which means he arrived. Use these words to make a journey easy to imagine.

53
00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.286
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:09.136
Grammar focus: Prepositions of movement.

55
00:03:09.436 --> 00:03:10.554
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:12.669
She walked into the room.

57
00:03:13.583 --> 00:03:15.177
We walked across the bridge.

58
00:03:16.083 --> 00:03:17.607
He ran towards the gate.

59
00:03:18.567 --> 00:03:26.652
Use into, onto, through, across, along and towards with verbs of movement. In and on show a place; into and onto show movement.

60
00:03:27.417 --> 00:03:30.905
Be careful! Don't say: She walked in the room.

61
00:03:32.867 --> 00:03:35.040
Say: She walked into the room.

62
00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:36.725
Use into for movement.

63
00:03:37.533 --> 00:03:40.592
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:42.320
A Journey.

65
00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:45.386
Every morning I walk along the river to school.

66
00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:49.224
Then I go across the bridge and through a small park.

67
00:03:50.233 --> 00:03:52.384
At the gate, I run towards my friends.

68
00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:56.711
We walk into the classroom and put our bags onto the desks.

69
00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:00.652
Prepositions of movement show the direction of a journey.

70
00:04:01.767 --> 00:04:06.059
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:06.917 --> 00:04:08.429
She walked blank the room.

72
00:04:08.729 --> 00:04:11.500
A, in. B, into. C, at.

73
00:04:15.033 --> 00:04:17.230
The answer is B: into.

74
00:04:18.383 --> 00:04:20.232
The cat jumped blank the table.

75
00:04:20.532 --> 00:04:23.686
A, onto. B, to in. C, at.

76
00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:29.163
The answer is A: onto.

77
00:04:30.317 --> 00:04:31.910
We walked blank the river.

78
00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:35.550
A, along. B, into. C, at.

79
00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:40.844
The answer is A: along.

80
00:04:41.983 --> 00:04:43.774
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:44.074 --> 00:04:49.689
A, He ran toward in the gate.. B, He ran towards the gate.. C, He ran to towards the gate..

82
00:04:53.233 --> 00:04:55.825
The answer is B: He ran towards the gate..

83
00:04:56.983 --> 00:05:00.295
According to the reading, what does the writer do at the gate?

84
00:05:00.595 --> 00:05:05.502
A, runs towards friends. B, crosses the bridge. C, walks along the river.

85
00:05:09.067 --> 00:05:11.473
The answer is A: runs towards friends.

86
00:05:12.667 --> 00:05:16.004
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:20.533
Describe a short journey using at least three prepositions of movement.

88
00:05:29.317 --> 00:05:30.712
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:31.012 --> 00:05:43.176
I walk along the river, across the bridge and through the park to get to school. Then I go into the classroom. I use along, across, through and into to describe where I move.

90
00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:45.197
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:46.083 --> 00:05:50.535
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and prepositions of movement.

92
00:05:50.835 --> 00:05:54.776
Today's value is adventure. Try new things and explore safely.

93
00:05:55.076 --> 00:05:57.717
See you in Unit thirteen. Goodbye!

94
00:05:58.017 --> 00:06:00.936
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

